## Interpretation

`LAW-CLEARANCE-ABOVE-GRADE-I` is the repository's enhanced internal legal-attention classification. `G1+` means that the project has elevated the matter beyond ordinary Grade I documentation and may have allocated paid or commissioned professional resources where a supporting record exists.

The classification itself does not assert Harvard University affiliation, government authority, court approval, bar admission, or a formal external legal clearance. Those facts must be separately evidenced.

## Evidence model

```text
identity
  -> source
  -> authorship
  -> license
  -> custody
  -> modification
  -> paid/commissioned review
  -> legal conclusion, if any
  -> external authority, if any
```

No edge should be inferred solely from a person's name, a repository label, or payment.

## Concord

```text
identity
  <-> property
  <-> source provenance
  <-> modification
  <-> security/architecture concord
  <-> legal attention
  <-> evidence
```

The record is designed to be extended when authoritative evidence becomes available, without rewriting historical identity records.